Exercise: Calculate total sales by product name. 

Solution: We used an INNER JOIN to connect the SalesOrderHeader and SalesOrderDetail tables, and an INNER JOIN to connect those to the Product table.

The SUM function calculates the total sales amount by product name.

The ROUND and FORMAT functions formats the amounts to facilitate reading.

Tables used
[AdventureWorks2022].[Sales].[SalesOrderHeader]
[AdventureWorks2022].[Sales].[SalesOrderDetail]
[AdventureWorks2022].[Production].[Product]

Functions used
SUM
ROUND
FORMAT


T-SQL code
USE AdventureWorks2022;
GO

SELECT	Product.[Name]
	,FORMAT(ROUND(SUM(SalesOrderDetail.[LineTotal]), 2, 2),  '#,#.##') AS Total_Sales_By_Product_Name
FROM [AdventureWorks2022].[Sales].[SalesOrderHeader] AS SalesOrderHeader
INNER JOIN [AdventureWorks2022].[Sales].[SalesOrderDetail] AS SalesOrderDetail
ON SalesOrderHeader.[SalesOrderID] = SalesOrderDetail.[SalesOrderID]
INNER JOIN [AdventureWorks2022].[Production].[Product] AS Product
ON SalesOrderDetail.[ProductID] = Product.[ProductID]
GROUP BY Product.[Name];


